    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The population of a sea lion colony decreases at a compound rate of $2\\%$ p.a. for $10$ years. If the population is $8000$ initially, what is it at the end of the $10$-year period? Give your answer to the nearest whole sea lion.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Approximately $6537$ sea lions.",
      "worked": "The population retains $100\\%-2\\%=98\\%$ each year.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{10}&=8000\\times(0.98)^{10}\\\\P_{10}&=6536.582455\\ldots\\\\P_{10}&\\approx6537\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population is approximately $6537$ sea lions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
